<%
// Custom listing template for the news index. Used by both index.qmd (six most
// recent) and news.qmd (everything), so the two stay identical by construction.
//
// Grey panels rather than hairline rows: a news item is a genuinely bounded
// object, which is the one place on this site where a panel is the honest form.
//
// The anchors are deliberately left on separate lines. Quarto runs this output
// back through Pandoc, which then wraps each anchor in a <p> — but it is also
// that same parse which rewrites the .qmd hrefs to .html. Emitting one long
// line avoids the <p> but loses link resolution, so the wrapper is absorbed in
// CSS instead (see .cbc-news > p in custom.scss).
%>
<div class="cbc-news">
<% for (const item of items) { %>
<a class="cbc-news-item" href="<%- item.path %>"><span class="cbc-news-date"><%= item.date %></span><span class="cbc-news-title"><%= item.title %></span></a>
<% } %>
</div>
